### 7. Overlaps the design should have cited (neutral)

- **`.planning/todos/pending/tre-linter-and-toc-set-builder.md`** — same scope; still says `buildTre` default was blocking (stale vs post-`1ecb559` state).
- **`DataPanel` / `IffStructureTree` / `iffStore`** — correct VFS lint UI seam, not `InspectorStack`.
- **`packages/harness/test/tre-builder-roundtrip.test.ts`** — build-twice determinism guard already in CI.
- **`packages/harness/test/tre-toc-extract-integration.test.ts`** — synthetic `.toc` + mount/extract chain.
- **`packagingArtifacts.ts` + `renderPolicyReport`** — existing human-readable report write pattern parallel to `manifest.ts` / compose reports.
- **`readVfsEntryBytes.ts`, `treMount.ts`, `treAutoMount.ts`** — mount/extract layer compose verify/UI will reuse.
- **`nativeTre.ts`** — renderer’s typed native facade vs raw `require`.
- **`policyEvaluator.ts`** — closer pure “evaluate + render report” analogue than full ruleset merge for lint v1.

---

## Minimal corrections to the design text

1. **§4 / lint registry:** Say merge by **`classId`** (or rename rules to carry a lint `ruleId` — not present today). Do not copy “rule id” wording from policy without noting the mismatch. Map severity to **`ban`/`advisory`** or define new lint severities explicitly in contracts.

2. **§8 / fixtures:** Change “existing sweep enforces” → “wire `assertSweep()` into CI” (or extend `registry-coverage.test.ts` to call it on `getRegistry()` after registrations). Today it does not run.

3. **§9 row 1:** Replace `InspectorStack` with **`DataPanel` / `IffStructureTree`** (and/or `VfsTree` row badges). Note prerequisite: propagate `parseIff().defects` through `iffStore` / `IffParseResult`.

4. **§9 row 2:** Winner archive is **already shown** in `VfsTree` (`winnerArchiveFilename`); revise “add to tooltip” to “extend detail panel / summary,” not greenfield chip work.

5. **§9 row 3:** Enumerate-only chip is **per-archive** (triggered by any per-entry extract failure), not per-payload chip on each row.

6. **§6:** Version token is on-disk **`"1000"`** (`0x30303031`), not `TAG_0001`, unless you explicitly equate engine macro names.

7. **§2 / CLI:** Document **`@swg/contracts` build step** (or tsconfig/vitest alias) for plain Node; no `"bin"` precedent exists yet.

8. **§3 pure moves:** Only **`crc32.ts`** and **`pathSafety.ts`** are move-ready; `tocReader.ts` and `clientSearchOrder.ts` need `fs` (+ layout) abstraction or stay wrapped.

9. **§6 / B0:** Reference harness **`buildSyntheticToc()`** as existing test-only `.toc` builder seed.

10. **§5 running-client lane:** Cite **fail-loud vs skipIf** split in harness; acknowledge **no running-client gate is implemented** yet in toolkit code.

11. **Stale todo cross-link:** Update or supersede `tre-linter-and-toc-set-builder.md` blocker text now that `buildTre('5000')` is the corrected default.
